<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schneeberg, Saxony</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schneeberg is a mining town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ore-mountains">Ore Mountains</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It grew rapidly after rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> finds from 1470 into one of the wealthiest towns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> silver boom, which financed the Wettin rulers. Later mining of cobalt, used for blue pigments, and in the twentieth century of uranium continued its industrial history, and its church of St Wolfgang holds an altarpiece from the Cranach workshop.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schneeberg-saxony.jpg" alt="Schneeberg, Saxony" width="299" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rauenstein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schneeberg_in_ERZ.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
